    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d331">

                <pb facs="0304" n="292" xml:id="pg292"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.91245/33: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-07-30T16:00:00+02:00">July 30, 1943—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 30—12:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4969. Department’s 3621, June 10, 10 p.m. We approached Foreign Office again on
                    United Press teletype telegraphic requirements in India and have just been told
                    that a definite reply from the Government of India was expected shortly.
                    Meanwhile, Foreign Office promises to continue to maintain pressure on
                    Government of India.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
